            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Both ['number'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c404fc5717866ff738aadeeb1f54ab8ed270ae1e/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1362) and ['relativenumber'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c404fc5717866ff738aadeeb1f54ab8ed270ae1e/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1364) are disabled in 'mini.starter' buffers. The reason for those still showing almost surely lies outside of 'mini.starter'.\r\n\r\nIn particular, there is [`vim.opt.relativenumber = true`](https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8bdb282016064e0302050edf120ff35762d09470/lua/options.lua#L4), which [gets executed `later`](https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8bdb282016064e0302050edf120ff35762d09470/init.lua#L207). This means that it sets relative number in current window also.\r\n\r\nThere are several ways to adjust this:\r\n- Use `vim.go.relativenumber = true` to explicitly set global value of this option. This won't affect currently opened window-buffers combinations, but should be used for future ones.\r\n- Set all options during startup (i.e. in `now` and not `later`), possibly even as one of the first things.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Both <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c404fc5717866ff738aadeeb1f54ab8ed270ae1e/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1362\">'number'</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c404fc5717866ff738aadeeb1f54ab8ed270ae1e/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1364\">'relativenumber'</a> are disabled in 'mini.starter' buffers. The reason for those still showing almost surely lies outside of 'mini.starter'.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In particular, there is <a href=\"https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8bdb282016064e0302050edf120ff35762d09470/lua/options.lua#L4\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.opt.relativenumber = true</code></a>, which <a href=\"https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8bdb282016064e0302050edf120ff35762d09470/init.lua#L207\">gets executed <code class=\"notranslate\">later</code></a>. This means that it sets relative number in current window also.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are several ways to adjust this:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Use <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.go.relativenumber = true</code> to explicitly set global value of this option. This won't affect currently opened window-buffers combinations, but should be used for future ones.</li>\n<li>Set all options during startup (i.e. in <code class=\"notranslate\">now</code> and not <code class=\"notranslate\">later</code>), possibly even as one of the first things.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Both 'number' and 'relativenumber' are disabled in 'mini.starter' buffers. The reason for those still showing almost surely lies outside of 'mini.starter'.\nIn particular, there is vim.opt.relativenumber = true, which gets executed later. This means that it sets relative number in current window also.\nThere are several ways to adjust this:\n\nUse vim.go.relativenumber = true to explicitly set global value of this option. This won't affect currently opened window-buffers combinations, but should be used for future ones.\nSet all options during startup (i.e. in now and not later), possibly even as one of the first things.",
